    "verdict": "FAILS_TO_SUPPORT",
    "verdict_statement": "The real-world PoseTrack21 VAL result FAILS TO SUPPORT the applicability-restricted spline claim. Every evaluated case satisfies the pre-frozen strict-interior condition, yet under that restriction spline is the WORST of the three classical operators (0.3204 against linear 0.2837 and Kalman 0.2857) and also carries the largest per-sequence maximum. It is beaten by linear at every gap length inside the primary grid.",
    "not_explained_by_anchor_scarcity": "anchor support is ample: 96.5 %, 96.8 %, 95.8 % and 95.7 % of cases at g=1,2,3,5 carry at least the four anchors the spline implementation requires, and 78.5 % of all cases carry twelve or more. Only 3.8 % of cases fall below four anchors, so the result is NOT a thin-anchor artefact. No mechanism is asserted beyond that.",
    "relation_to_earlier_results": {
      "3dpw_t4_conclusion_rewritten": false,
      "jta_record_51_recomputed": false,
      "statement": "On JTA (record 51) spline was the BEST classical operator under the same kind of pre-frozen interior restriction; on NTU (record 45) it was by far the worst family in the noise-amplification estimand. PoseTrack21 lands with NTU in ordering, not with JTA. These are three populations under two different estimands and no unified claim is made here; the earlier 3DPW T4 conclusion and JTA record 51 are quoted, not rewritten."
    }
