    "q1_does_correction_remove_the_jta_style_failure": {
      "answer": "PARTIALLY, AND NOT ATTRIBUTABLY",
      "detail": "the magnitude collapses: on JTA the same frozen checkpoints scored MAE 14.86 and BiGRU 27.30-27.76 torso lengths; on PoseTrack21 VAL under the corrected contract they score MAE 2.41 and BiGRU 3.87-4.06. The catastrophic regime is gone. But this is NOT a controlled comparison: the population changed AND the inference contract changed at the same time, so the improvement cannot be attributed to the correction alone. The only controlled evidence for the correction is the verification suite, which shows it is exactly a no-op where training and old inference already agreed and exactly window-local where they did not.",
      "causality_claimed": false
    },
    "q2_finite_and_scale_plausible": {
      "answer": "YES",
      "detail": "every learned case error is finite. The per-sequence MEDIAN is 0.5330 for MAE and about 1.5684 for BiGRU \u2014 around half a torso length and one and a half torso lengths respectively, which is physically plausible. The MEAN is far higher (2.41 and 3.87-4.06) because the per-sequence distribution is heavily right-skewed, with maxima of 41.5 and 62.2. Both the mean and the dispersion are reported; neither is suppressed."
    },
    "q3_does_the_ntu_learned_direction_remain": {
      "answer": "NO \u2014 IT INVERTS",
      "ntu_reference_record_45_beta_phi0": {
        "linear": 0.6049,
        "spline": 10.54643,
        "kalman": 1.43686,
        "mae": 0.11684,
        "bigru_seed0": 0.07856,
        "bigru_seed1": 0.07496,
        "bigru_seed2": 0.09015
      },
      "estimand_caveat": "record 45 reports beta, the noise-amplification slope from the E5 sigma sweep, NOT a torso-normalized reconstruction error. No sigma sweep is applicable to PoseTrack21 (no jitter rule is frozen for it, exactly as for JTA), so this is an ORDERING comparison across two different estimands and not a like-for-like magnitude comparison.",
      "detail": "on NTU the learned family sat BELOW every classical operator (BiGRU 0.075-0.090 < MAE 0.117 < linear 0.605 < Kalman 1.437 < spline 10.546). On PoseTrack21 VAL the ordering is linear 0.2837 < Kalman 0.2857 < spline 0.3204 << MAE 2.4062 < BiGRU 3.8652-4.0552. The learned family moves from best to worst, and within it BiGRU and MAE swap places: BiGRU led on NTU, MAE leads here."
    },
    "q4_population_shift_vs_preprocessing": {
